    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9547" root="حوف" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَافٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَافَةٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>A certain vein, of a green
colour,</i> or <i>of a dark,</i> or <i>an ashy, dust-colour,</i>
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْضَرُ</span>,) <i>beneath the tongue:</i> (O, Msb:) there
are two veins of this description, called the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَافَانِ</span>:
(K:) accord. to some, the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ف</span> is with teshdeed.
(TA.)

